 "brief": "Wordless paper-cut illustration (19.62 s) for a Short or a re-edit of a published explainer on tool calling. A courier (the agent loop) wheels a cart of pages from a tool hatch to a seated reader (the model). Each turn a new page drops from the hatch onto the pile, the whole pile goes back to the reader, who reads every page and pays one coin per page into a cost jar beside him; a strip per turn on a cork board grows 1..5 into a staircase, outlined as a triangle, next to a flat grey dashed row of equal strips (the linear intuition).",
